device_id,device_ip,management_type,iris_vlan,svi_ip,svi_mask,app_ip,app_mask,app_gateway,inband_vlan,ios_ssh_host,model,platform
# One row per device — NETWORK INFO ONLY. Tokens and secrets are handled
# automatically by the Console/API onboarding flow (see the Management Type
# and VLAN Ownership doc). Comment lines (#) and the header are ignored on import.
#
# management_type (required): 'routed' or 'inband'.
#   routed  = IRIS creates a dedicated VLAN + SVI. Fill iris_vlan, svi_ip,
#             svi_mask, app_ip, app_mask, app_gateway. Leave inband_vlan blank.
#   inband  = attach to an EXISTING operator-owned VLAN. IRIS never creates,
#             changes, or removes that VLAN/SVI/gateway/routes/VRF. Fill
#             inband_vlan, app_ip, app_mask, app_gateway. Leave iris_vlan/svi_* blank.
# 'model' is OPTIONAL (e.g. C9300-48UXM, IE-3400); blank lets onboarding detect it.
# 'platform' is OPTIONAL and LAST: blank = auto (by model), or force 'guestshell'
#   or 'iox'. Inband supports Guest Shell and IOx (IE-3x00, C9300); DHCP is NOT
#   supported and is rejected on import.
# ios_ssh_host: OPTIONAL for inband IOx. The app SSHes to the switch's mgmt IP
#   (device_ip) by default; set this only to override it. Blank for Guest Shell.
#
# Routed example (dedicated IRIS VLAN/SVI):
100.92.9.3,100.92.9.3,routed,666,100.92.9.125,255.255.255.252,100.92.9.126,255.255.255.252,100.92.9.125,,,C9300-48UXM,guestshell
# Inband Guest Shell example (existing management VLAN 120, static address):
100.92.9.1,100.92.9.1,inband,,,,100.92.9.121,255.255.255.0,100.92.9.1,120,,C9300-48UXM,guestshell
# Inband IOx example (IE-3400, app SSHes to the existing management SVI 100.90.168.98):
100.90.168.99,100.90.168.99,inband,,,,100.90.168.97,255.255.255.0,100.90.168.98,120,100.90.168.98,IE-3400,iox
